    j = j + "  \"verdict_rule\": \"PASS iff F_NONNEG AND F_GE4 AND F_COUNT127 AND F_SPECIAL AND F_DET; F_SPECIAL = peak (Φ(K=8) strictly > Φ(K=4) AND > Φ(K=16)) OR plateau-onset (Φ(K=8) >= Φ(K=4) AND |Φ(K=8)-Φ(K=16)| <= 0.5 Φ(K=8) AND Φ(K=8) > 0)\",\n"
    j = j + "  \"verdict\": \"" + verdict + "\",\n"
    j = j + "  \"criterion\": \"H_171.1 substrate-side ONLY — empirical F1 (cortical mini-column stereology meta) UNADDRESSED here\",\n"
    j = j + "  \"honest_limits\": [\n"
    j = j + "    \"L1: This is a SUBSTRATE-Φ measurement on an abstract logistic-ring lattice — it does NOT prove K=8 is the biological consciousness atom. The empirical F1 falsifier in H_171 (cortical mini-column stereology median sub-module count in [6,10] across V1/S1/M1/PFC) is NOT addressed; this cycle only tests one substrate-consistency leg of H_171.1. The biological-vs-substrate category boundary is intact (raw#91 c3 candor).\",\n"
    j = j + "    \"L2: phi_spatial = 🟢 NUMERICAL spatial-slice replica of phi_rs (RFC 036), NOT full IIT 4.0 — no system-level Φ partition search, no cause-effect structure, no exclusion postulate. The 'MIP-like' bipartition enumeration here uses a cheap cross-boundary variance surrogate (NOT Earth-Mover distance / NOT IIT 4.0 phi_MIP) — it is used ONLY to verify the bipartition COUNT (127), not to compete with phi_spatial as the Φ measurement.\",\n"
    j = j + "    \"L3: K=8 'specialness' is operationalised as peak OR plateau-onset against K=4 / K=16 with a 50% relative tolerance — both criteria are design choices, not derived from theory. A different specialness rule (e.g. local maximum across {6,8,10}, or coefficient-of-variation threshold) could change the verdict. The K=8 prediction is also pre-registered as sopfr(8)=6 perfect-class universal (L1 in H_171), which is NUMBER-THEORETIC, not dynamical — the present substrate test cannot distinguish 'K=8 atom' from 'any-K-with-enough-cells plateau'.\",\n"
    j = j + "    \"L4: model = chaotic logistic map (r=3.85) + nn diffusion (0.08). This was chosen for sustained non-degenerate trajectories so phi_spatial has signal; it is NOT a neural model. Any K-special signature here is a property of the logistic ring, NOT of cortical mini-columns. A different substrate (Kuramoto / Wilson-Cowan / integrate-fire) could give a different K-profile.\",\n"
    j = j + "    \"L5: WARM=8 + DIM=12 + N_SEEDS=5 are inherited from H_007 (a small / fast configuration). The K-sweep is over only 6 K values {4,6,8,10,12,16}; finer sweeps (K=5,7,9,11,13,14,15) or larger DIM/WARM could change the plateau/peak structure. seed_base alone is varied; rotor/init class is not.\",\n"
    j = j + "    \"L6: The 2^(K-1)-1 closed form for bipartition count is reproduced empirically by the enumerator (K=4 -> 7, K=6 -> 31, K=8 -> 127); `hexa verify --expr` has no path for 'pow' (returned 🟠 INSUFFICIENT — see verbatim_hexa_verify.note), so the formal-identity tier is fenced to ⚪ via `hexa verify --fence` (verdict VERBATIM in result.json) rather than promoted to 🔵. The empirical enumeration agreement is the SUPPORTED leg.\",\n"
    j = j + "    \"L7: H_171's other 3 predictions (F_c=0.10 / split-brain non-conservation / 1/f thalamus) are NOT touched by this cycle. F5 (4-prediction independence) and F6 (E:I canonical conflict) likewise unaddressed. The §Criteria table for H_171 is updated only at C1's substrate-side leg; C2-C4 remain pending and C5 (n=6 perfect-class binding) carries unchanged.\"\n"
    j = j + "  ]\n"
    j = j + "}\n"
    write_file(_state_dir() + "/result.json", j)

    println("")
    println("  result.json written → " + _state_dir() + "/result.json")
    println("=== H_171 Cycle #1 K=8 atom substrate-Φ smoke complete: " + verdict + " ===")
}
